From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teddy Astie <teddy.astie@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:08:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ensure passed ring-page-order is valid

The current logic accepts any guest provided ring order, which can cause a
stack overflow in tap_ctl_connect_xenblkif() as tapdisk_message_blkif::gref
can only store 8 grant references, yet order may be larger than 3.

Fix this by checking that ring order values is in [0..3] range.  Also clarify
the gref array size in tapdisk_message_blkif (fixes TODO).

This is XSA-521 / CVE-2026-102701.

Signed-off-by: Teddy Astie <teddy.astie@vates.tech>
Reviewed-by: Ross Lagerwall <ross.lagerwall@citrix.com>
Tested-by: Alex Brett <alex.brett@citrix.com>
---
 control/tap-ctl-xen.c | 6 +++++-
 tapback/frontend.c    | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/control/tap-ctl-xen.c b/control/tap-ctl-xen.c
index 14c60ec4..81f5dcbe 100644
--- a/control/tap-ctl-xen.c
+++ b/control/tap-ctl-xen.c
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+#include "xen_blkif.h"
+#include "debug.h"
 #include "tap-ctl.h"
 #include "compiler.h"
 #include "util.h"
@@ -58,7 +60,9 @@ tap_ctl_connect_xenblkif(const pid_t pid, const domid_t domid, const int devid,
     tapdisk_message_t message;
     int i, err;
 
-	memset(&message, 0, sizeof(message));
+    ASSERT(order >= 0 && order <= MAX_RING_PAGE_ORDER);
+
+    memset(&message, 0, sizeof(message));
     message.type = TAPDISK_MESSAGE_XENBLKIF_CONNECT;
     message.cookie = minor;
 
diff --git a/tapback/frontend.c b/tapback/frontend.c
index e086813e..65b8ffca 100644
--- a/tapback/frontend.c
+++ b/tapback/frontend.c
@@ -119,6 +119,12 @@ connect_tap(vbd_t * const device)
                 "%d", &order))
         order = 0;
 
+    if (order < 0 || order > MAX_RING_PAGE_ORDER) {
+        WARN(device, "front-end asked for an invalid ring order: %d\n", order);
+        err = EINVAL;
+        goto out;
+    }
+
      nr_pages = 1 << order;
 
     if (!(gref = calloc(nr_pages, sizeof(grant_ref_t)))) {
